  "source": "USPS three-digit ZIP Code prefixes by state (the first three digits of a five-digit ZIP), as assigned in USPS Publication 28 and the National ZIP Code directory. Recalled from that assignment table, not transcribed from it.",
  "confidence": "unverified",
  "confidenceNote": "The state boundaries of the three-digit prefixes are stable and well known, but this list was written from memory and NOT checked prefix by prefix against the USPS table. A few prefixes straddle a border (201 is Virginia inside the DC block, 733 and 885 are Texas inside Oklahoma's and New Mexico's blocks). Territories, military and unique prefixes are left out on purpose, so a ZIP outside the fifty states and DC gives no suggestion rather than a wrong one. verify: true.",
  "verify": true,
  "note": "ranges are inclusive three-digit prefixes [from, to, state]; the FIRST matching range wins, which is why the two Texas exceptions sit above the ranges they cut into. Read by shared/suggest.js (rule zipToState) to SUGGEST a state from a ZIP; the person confirms it. D-205.",
